# AEE Bootstrap v1 — Python runtime requirements manifest (spec §6.1, §6.3).
#
# This is the bootstrap-manifest copy of the repo's runtime Python deps.
# The canonical source for runtime deps is the repo-root
# ``requirements.in`` / ``requirements.lock``; this manifest exists so
# the bootstrap layer has a single self-contained manifests/ tree (spec
# §3 layout) and the future ``aee doctor --reproducibility`` check can
# verify the lock hash without reaching outside ``bootstrap/``.
#
# Format: one requirement per line, compatible with ``uv pip install
# -r``. No version pins here — the lockfile (python.requirements.lock)
# is the source of truth for pinned versions + hashes.
#
# Spec §6.1 hard deps:
#   * No additional Python hard deps beyond the runtime's own
#     requirements. The bootstrap itself is stdlib-only (lifecycle,
#     redaction, detect all use only Python stdlib).
#
# Spec §6.2 profile-gated:
#   * ``full`` / ``edge`` — no extra Python deps (Docker is system-level).
#   * ``mini`` — no extra Python deps (supervisor is system-level apt/brew).
#   * ``developer`` — no extra Python deps (Node.js is system-level).
#
# This manifest intentionally mirrors ``../../requirements.in`` so the
# bootstrap layer is self-describing. When the repo's runtime deps
# change, this file and ``python.requirements.lock`` MUST be regenerated
# via ``uv pip compile -o bootstrap/manifests/python.requirements.lock
# bootstrap/manifests/python.requirements.in``.

fastapi
uvicorn[standard]
httpx
python-dotenv
pydantic